  "experience": {
    "narrative": "You push through the crowd at Trattoria da Enzo al 29, where the scene is chaotic in the best way—locals dominating every table, conversation flowing in rapid-fire local dialect, and zero concessions to tourist comfort. The Cacio e pepe arrives, and you understand why people make pilgrimages here—every element is precisely executed, ingredients at their peak, technique honed over years. House wine from owner's cousin's vineyard in frascati makes this more than just a meal; it's an immersion into the authentic culture of the place. This is the kind of dining that reminds you why you seek out local favorites, why recommendations from residents are gold, why some restaurants transcend mere eating to become essential experiences.",
    "rating": 4.6
  }
